rs  i think learners are more independent  yet they still require the help of of  teachers to move them along  but that and therefore all of this is  making language learning easier and  therefore i think that  that  the new role of teachers and the  technology that's available is going to  make people learn languages more quickly  more easily  and therefore more people will learn  languages because  the joy is accessing  this other world reading listening  speaking sitting down over  a cup of coffee with someone and  conversing comfortably in another  language understanding more about them  and their culture or  simply in an event like this press  conference  uh  you know if you're not everyone's going  to be the president of france or the  president of the united states but  imagine that the president of the united  states there  were able to answer a question in french  i mean they have simultaneous  interpreters  i just find that that whole environment  is so  um  stimulating  and rewarding  that people will want to do that people  will want to  have that sense of achievement of having  learned another language being able to  use it being able to communicate in it  and just having some  technology that enables you to  communicate  is not going to do it  i think if you're going as i said in my  interview if you're going to croatia  rather than buying a phrasebook you  might buy some or you might have some  app that enables you to order a beer  but  uh you know the fact that we have four  by four altering  vehicles and stuff has not meant that  there's less interest in hiking  uh in fact we have hiking and we have  mountain bikes and we have so many other  ways in which people enjoy  getting into the um  you know the wilderness  and similarly with languages the more  the easier it becomes to learn languages  the more  uh enjoyable the language learning uh  process becomes as people are able to  use the various different apps and  resources on the internet to more 